{
  "sql": "SELECT i.snapshot_date AS snapshot_date, i.product_id AS product_id, p.product_name AS product_name, i.days_of_supply AS days_of_supply FROM commerce.inventory AS i JOIN commerce.products AS p ON i.product_id = p.product_id WHERE i.snapshot_date = (SELECT MAX(j.snapshot_date) FROM commerce.inventory AS j) AND i.days_of_supply IS NOT NULL ORDER BY 4 ASC LIMIT 10",
  "parameters": [],
  "explanation": "Selects the 10 products with the lowest non-null stored days_of_supply at the latest inventory snapshot. The query joins inventory to products to retrieve product names, filters to the latest snapshot date using a subquery, excludes null days_of_supply values, and orders by the metric in ascending position."
}

